^SAMPLE = GSM8340249
!Sample_title = PA treated HepG2 cells for Cur and copper incubation_2
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM8340249
!Sample_status = Public on Jun 19 2026
!Sample_submission_date = Jun 20 2024
!Sample_last_update_date = Jun 19 2026
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = liver
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: liver
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: HepG2
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: Human hepatocellular carcinomas
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: cancer cell
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: Cur-Cu + PA
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = For PA group, The HepG2 cells pre-treated with 750 μM for 24h. For PA-Cur group, the cells pre-treated with 750 μM for 24h, were then incubated with 20 μM Cur for 12 h. For PA-Cur-Cu group, the PA-treated HepG2 cells were co-treated with Cur (20 µM) and CuCl2 (5 µM) for 12 h.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = HepG2 cells were gifted by Dr. Hongmin Zhang [Department of Infectious Diseases, Institute for Viral Hepatitis, Key Laboratory of Molecular Biology for Infectious Diseases (Ministry of Education), Chongqing, China] and cultured in Dulbecco's modified Eagle's medium (DMEM; Gibco Life Science, Grand Island, NY, USA) containing 10% fetal bovine serum and 1% penicillin-streptomycin (Beyotime, Shanghai, China), at 37°C in a 95%-O2 and 5%-CO2 atmosphere.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA was harvested using TRIzol (Takara, Shiga, Japan). 1.0 ug of total RNA was used for the construction of sequencing libraries.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA libraries for RNA-seq were prepared using Illumina® Stranded mRNA Prep, Ligation according to manufacturer’s recommendations.
!Sample_data_processing = Through removing low quality, ploy-N, and adapter contained reads by in-house perl scripts, high-quality clean data were used for further analysis.
!Sample_data_processing = After building index of the reference genome (GRCh38.p13), paired-end clean reads were aligned to the mouse genome using Hisat (v2.1.0).
!Sample_data_processing = For the quantification of gene expression, RSEM (v1.3.3) was used to count the clean reads numbers mapped to each gene, and the TPM (transcripts per million reads) value of each gene was obtained according to the gene length and reads count.
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: GRCh38.p13
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Text file include all TPM values for each Sample
